1
00:00:02,035 --> 00:00:03,367
GORDON: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:04,838 --> 00:00:07,467
GORDON: <i>I'm arresting you for
the murder of the boy you blew up</i>

3
00:00:07,541 --> 00:00:09,032
<i>under the Crown Point Bridge.</i>

4
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:11,338
And how can you help me?

5
00:00:11,979 --> 00:00:14,210
What do you say,
pal? Give me a smile...

6
00:00:14,381 --> 00:00:15,474
(LAUGHS)

7
00:00:15,716 --> 00:00:18,083
BRUCE: <i>I'm not who my
parents might've wanted me to be.</i>

8
00:00:18,185 --> 00:00:20,484
- And I'm okay with that.
- I'm not okay with it.

9
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:23,248
I went to my lawyer to have
him draw up emancipation papers.

10
00:00:23,557 --> 00:00:24,923
Alfred, you're fired.

11
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:26,323
<i>Now get the hell
out of my house.</i>

12
00:00:26,727 --> 00:00:28,320
I am in control!

13
00:00:28,395 --> 00:00:29,658
But why would you want that?

14
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:32,165
We had so much
fun when we were me.

15
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:34,824
- MAN: Surprise.
- (GUN COCKS)

16
00:00:35,402 --> 00:00:37,180
SOFIA: I needed the
police to turn on Penguin.

17
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:39,070
So you sent this
monster to my city?

18
00:00:39,172 --> 00:00:40,231
(GUNSHOT)

19
00:00:42,009 --> 00:00:44,308
I need you at the
head of the GCPD.

20
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:45,676
Let them think you're a hero.

21
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:49,072
This is Gordon. I just
shot and killed the Pyg.

22
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,684
SELINA: <i>Ivy?</i>

23
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:54,753
<i>What happened to you?</i>

24
00:00:54,855 --> 00:00:56,255
IVY: <i>I've been reborn.</i>

25
00:00:56,523 --> 00:00:58,389
(YELLS AND GROANS)

26
00:00:58,759 --> 00:01:00,853
IVY: <i>And I will never
be underestimated</i>

27
00:01:00,928 --> 00:01:02,829
or ignored ever again.

28
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,092
Let's make Gotham our bitch.

29
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:20,213
(BUZZER RINGS)

30
00:01:23,417 --> 00:01:24,885
Can I help you?

31
00:01:30,891 --> 00:01:32,951
You're so beautiful.

32
00:01:34,061 --> 00:01:35,120
Thanks.

33
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:36,624
Now, move.

34
00:01:40,267 --> 00:01:41,711
BOY: <i>Hey, Dad, guess what
happened at school today.</i>

35
00:01:41,735 --> 00:01:42,946
GIRL: <i>Oh, my God,
you're gonna love this.</i>

36
00:01:42,970 --> 00:01:44,447
BOY: <i>Can I just tell him?</i>
GIRL: <i>Wait. No, can I tell him?</i>

37
00:01:44,471 --> 00:01:45,530
BOY: Just let me tell him.

38
00:01:45,606 --> 00:01:46,630
Nice score.

39
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:49,266
Cindy, who are these two...

40
00:01:53,146 --> 00:01:57,777
Well, what a
charming young lady.

41
00:01:57,851 --> 00:01:59,945
She's so beautiful, Mom.

42
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:02,580
- That's cool.
- So your perfume

43
00:02:02,656 --> 00:02:05,091
turns people into
your super fans?

44
00:02:05,158 --> 00:02:07,252
Like all good
things, it'll fade.

45
00:02:07,327 --> 00:02:08,327
But until then,

46
00:02:08,996 --> 00:02:09,996
they're mine.

47
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:12,728
Freeze.

48
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:27,942
Not bad.

49
00:02:28,682 --> 00:02:30,548
I'll check out the
rest of the house.

50
00:02:38,959 --> 00:02:41,428
My friend thinks
we're here to rob you.

51
00:02:42,129 --> 00:02:43,688
But I know who you work for,

52
00:02:43,797 --> 00:02:46,266
Roland Charles, PhD.

53
00:02:50,037 --> 00:02:55,635
How you torture plants
in the name of science.

54
00:03:07,888 --> 00:03:10,790
Do you ever wonder
how those plants feel?

55
00:03:13,794 --> 00:03:17,561
Soon, you'll share
more with them

56
00:03:18,231 --> 00:03:21,224
than you ever could've imagined.

57
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:25,034
(GRUNTS)

58
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:32,342
(GROANS)

59
00:03:39,086 --> 00:03:40,486
What did you do to him?

60
00:03:41,421 --> 00:03:43,515
I gave him what he deserves.

61
00:03:44,257 --> 00:03:45,987
(ROLAND CHOKING)

62
00:04:05,779 --> 00:04:09,341
MAN: Captain, Captain
Gordon. Yoo hoo.

63
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:12,075
Captain, Captain Gordon.

64
00:04:12,185 --> 00:04:13,619
Chaz Carmichael.

65
00:04:13,887 --> 00:04:16,220
- Congratulations.
- The Boss ain't gonna be happy

66
00:04:16,289 --> 00:04:17,289
I'm in here.

67
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:18,501
Let's say I got a
lot of responsibility

68
00:04:18,525 --> 00:04:19,891
in my organization.

69
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:22,054
Well, you seem like
a real responsible guy.

70
00:04:22,129 --> 00:04:24,963
My boss is Sofia Falcone.

71
00:04:30,804 --> 00:04:32,739
Oh, yeah? What's
that got to do with me?

72
00:04:32,806 --> 00:04:35,970
Easy, all I know is, she
told me, if I ever got pinched,

73
00:04:36,143 --> 00:04:37,509
to tell you to give her a call.

74
00:04:39,546 --> 00:04:40,546
Is that so?

75
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:41,858
You can't do this. I got rights!

76
00:04:41,882 --> 00:04:44,242
Oh yeah, how about you
exercise your right to remain silent?

77
00:04:44,818 --> 00:04:46,081
Hey, Cap.

78
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:48,884
Got something.

79
00:04:49,756 --> 00:04:53,818
Victim is Roland Charles, over in
R&D, Wayne Enterprises Biotech.

80
00:04:53,927 --> 00:04:55,505
Did you know him from
when you worked at Wayne?

81
00:04:55,529 --> 00:04:58,522
I met him in passing, not that
I recognized him right away.

82
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:03,035
LUCIUS: It's like the
tweaker we found last week.

83
00:05:03,603 --> 00:05:04,680
The toxin entered
the bloodstream

84
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:06,002
through the cuts on the neck.

85
00:05:06,173 --> 00:05:09,007
If it is the same as the last
victim, the toxin creates vines

86
00:05:09,109 --> 00:05:10,668
that feed off of
the victim's body,

87
00:05:10,777 --> 00:05:12,177
while also attacking
the hippocampus

88
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:14,339
like some plant-based
psychedelics.

89
00:05:14,447 --> 00:05:17,007
GORDON: So it kills you
and makes you hallucinate?

90
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:20,444
- Any witnesses?
- LUCIUS: The family is saying

91
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,613
that it was two women.

92
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:22,815
Redhead and a brunette.

93
00:05:22,923 --> 00:05:25,290
The redhead used some
kind of hypnosis on them,

94
00:05:25,358 --> 00:05:27,020
and the brunette
wore a leather whip.

95
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:29,026
Selina Kyle?

96
00:05:30,030 --> 00:05:31,692
Murder's not really her thing.

97
00:05:31,798 --> 00:05:33,892
The family says the
redhead killed Roland.

98
00:05:34,067 --> 00:05:35,228
She left with his briefcase.

99
00:05:37,137 --> 00:05:38,366
If his briefcase is missing,

100
00:05:38,471 --> 00:05:39,782
maybe this is
related to his work

101
00:05:39,806 --> 00:05:41,468
- at Wayne Biotech?
- Doubtful.

102
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:45,308
He oversaw standard projects,
pharmaceuticals, pesticides.

103
00:05:47,647 --> 00:05:48,842
What?

104
00:05:49,115 --> 00:05:50,115
Nothing.

105
00:05:51,718 --> 00:05:53,209
I'll track down Selina.

106
00:05:59,726 --> 00:06:00,921
(SIGHS)

107
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:03,488
BRUCE: (ON VOICEMAIL)
<i>This is Bruce. Leave a message.</i>

108
00:06:04,264 --> 00:06:06,324
Bruce, I know we
haven't talked in a while.

109
00:06:06,399 --> 00:06:09,233
But someone just
killed Roland Charles.

110
00:06:09,736 --> 00:06:11,432
We may have a problem.

111
00:06:15,842 --> 00:06:17,333
Roland Charles
asked for clearance

112
00:06:17,410 --> 00:06:20,346
for some top-secret
biotech experiment.

113
00:06:21,748 --> 00:06:22,841
Project M.

114
00:06:22,916 --> 00:06:24,578
Ivy, do you think
I care about that?

115
00:06:25,252 --> 00:06:28,745
You just killed a man
in front of his family.

116
00:06:29,256 --> 00:06:33,023
He had it coming. You have
no idea what these people do.

117
00:06:35,462 --> 00:06:38,591
We need to find out everything
we can about Project M.

118
00:06:39,299 --> 00:06:40,790
And whatever it is,

119
00:06:41,101 --> 00:06:44,401
all access would've had to have
been approved by Bruce Wayne.

120
00:06:44,504 --> 00:06:46,735
You know, I really thought

121
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,537
that doing a crime spree
with you would be fun.

122
00:06:50,010 --> 00:06:51,103
But...

123
00:06:51,211 --> 00:06:52,770
(GRUNTS) I was wrong.

124
00:06:53,446 --> 00:06:55,381
- Selina.
- Leave me alone.

125
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,015
Enjoy your shrubs.

126
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:03,921
(DOOR CLOSES)

127
00:07:07,661 --> 00:07:08,924
We don't need her.

128
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:16,392
Now let's show everyone
just how strong we are.

129
00:07:24,144 --> 00:07:26,636
(COCKATOO CROWING)

130
00:07:27,747 --> 00:07:30,979
COCKATOO: Pour me another
shot. Pour me another shot.

131
00:07:31,251 --> 00:07:33,277
(TRILLING)

132
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:35,645
(WHISTLES)

133
00:07:35,755 --> 00:07:37,621
- Party time.
- (GROANS)

134
00:07:37,824 --> 00:07:39,486
Party time.

135
00:07:40,927 --> 00:07:42,987
- Shut up.
- COCKATOO: Gonna throw up.

136
00:07:43,596 --> 00:07:44,596
Gonna throw up.

137
00:07:44,831 --> 00:07:46,663
IVY: You know, I've
had some crazy nights.

138
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,935
But I've never
bought a talking bird.

139
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:52,969
Sorry, party's over.

140
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:54,340
I wasn't at the party.

141
00:07:57,677 --> 00:07:59,111
I've seen you before.

142
00:08:00,447 --> 00:08:02,848
At The Sirens. What
are you doing here?

143
00:08:06,019 --> 00:08:08,818
I'm here to speak for those

144
00:08:08,888 --> 00:08:10,789
who can't speak for
themselves, Bruce.

145
00:08:10,857 --> 00:08:13,725
I'm here to speak
for the plants.

146
00:08:15,528 --> 00:08:16,860
Okay.

147
00:08:18,198 --> 00:08:21,168
My head hurts. Please get out.

148
00:08:26,272 --> 00:08:27,433
First,

149
00:08:28,608 --> 00:08:30,372
tell me about Project M.

150
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,175
How do you know about that?

151
00:08:35,248 --> 00:08:37,149
Oh, I know a lot of things,

152
00:08:38,885 --> 00:08:40,877
billionaire boy.

153
00:08:42,489 --> 00:08:43,582
Ivy?

154
00:08:49,662 --> 00:08:53,656
You're so beautiful.

155
00:08:54,167 --> 00:08:55,931
Now, Project M.

156
00:08:58,905 --> 00:09:01,340
(CROWS CAWING)

157
00:09:01,908 --> 00:09:04,002
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

158
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:18,419
Hi, guys.

159
00:09:19,359 --> 00:09:20,359
Get it off!

160
00:09:35,442 --> 00:09:37,377
Is this seat taken?

161
00:09:37,444 --> 00:09:39,208
If I say "yes," will it
make a difference?

162
00:09:39,646 --> 00:09:41,547
You know, I've
always been a fan.

163
00:09:41,614 --> 00:09:43,879
When you got locked
up in this loony bin,

164
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:47,614
I expected great
things, a murder or two,

165
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:50,451
maybe a prison break.

166
00:09:51,891 --> 00:09:56,556
But all you've done is
mope for the last six weeks.

167
00:09:58,431 --> 00:09:59,729
(WINCES)

168
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,732
You must know I cannot escape.

169
00:10:01,801 --> 00:10:02,996
Why?

170
00:10:05,171 --> 00:10:06,469
None of your business.

171
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,068
(GROANING)

172
00:10:09,142 --> 00:10:12,306
Because Sofia Falcone is holding
someone important to me captive.

173
00:10:12,412 --> 00:10:13,971
And if I escape,
she will kill him.

174
00:10:14,247 --> 00:10:17,445
(YAWNING) Wow,
what a boring story.

175
00:10:17,650 --> 00:10:22,145
If there's one thing I can't
stand, it's someone boring.

176
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:26,485
The last person who
bored me was Dietrich.

177
00:10:27,594 --> 00:10:30,223
- Dietrich.
- I had to sneak into his shock therapy

178
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:32,265
session and goose the juice.

179
00:10:32,732 --> 00:10:36,066
Now he pees himself 10 times
a day and sometimes, uh...

180
00:10:38,872 --> 00:10:41,137
Poos himself. (CHUCKLES)

181
00:10:44,777 --> 00:10:46,541
Well, that's very sad.

182
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:51,348
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

183
00:10:52,619 --> 00:10:55,282
I'm gonna cure you
of this attitude, Oswald.

184
00:10:58,057 --> 00:11:00,117
I'm gonna find that
entertaining guy

185
00:11:00,193 --> 00:11:02,219
I know is inside of you.

186
00:11:02,695 --> 00:11:04,891
And when I do, ooh,

187
00:11:05,632 --> 00:11:09,194
we are gonna have
so much fun together.

188
00:11:15,542 --> 00:11:17,374
That's quite a story.

189
00:11:18,945 --> 00:11:20,436
Not what I was expecting.

190
00:11:22,048 --> 00:11:23,448
You're just so easy to talk to.

191
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:28,017
Normally, I'd make this quick

192
00:11:28,121 --> 00:11:29,282
like I did with Roland.

193
00:11:29,722 --> 00:11:31,486
But it's your name
on the company

194
00:11:31,558 --> 00:11:33,527
that murders my
little green friends.

195
00:11:34,227 --> 00:11:36,059
I'm so sorry, Ivy.

196
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:39,494
I would never want to upset you.

197
00:11:39,566 --> 00:11:41,057
But you have, Bruce.

198
00:11:43,937 --> 00:11:45,735
Hide out here all you want.

199
00:11:49,242 --> 00:11:51,609
Bury your head in the sand.

200
00:11:55,014 --> 00:11:56,448
You're still guilty.

201
00:12:01,254 --> 00:12:02,347
(GASPS)

202
00:12:08,561 --> 00:12:09,859
It'll be slow.

203
00:12:11,531 --> 00:12:12,931
And it'll be painful.

204
00:12:15,435 --> 00:12:16,926
But it's what you deserve.

205
00:12:19,339 --> 00:12:20,671
- (GROANS)
- (BODY THUDS)

206
00:12:21,608 --> 00:12:24,043
(WHEEZING)

207
00:12:26,879 --> 00:12:29,713
I'm just sorry I won't be
here to see you bloom.

208
00:12:30,516 --> 00:12:31,950
(CHOKING)

209
00:12:36,356 --> 00:12:37,756
(GASPING)

210
00:12:46,733 --> 00:12:48,895
(GASPING)

211
00:12:57,410 --> 00:12:59,936
Nope, nope.

212
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:03,472
No. None of these will do.

213
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:04,978
Where's Ivy?

214
00:13:05,084 --> 00:13:07,110
What did she do
to me? Where am I?

215
00:13:07,186 --> 00:13:08,245
Ah!

216
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:10,622
Just the thing.

217
00:13:10,990 --> 00:13:12,151
Ra's al Ghul?

218
00:13:12,592 --> 00:13:14,458
Ra's al Ghul?

219
00:13:14,661 --> 00:13:15,959
Nope, never heard of him.

220
00:13:16,062 --> 00:13:19,396
I'm Dr. Greenthumb, just here
to do a little light pruning, really.

221
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:20,489
No!

222
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,898
No!

223
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:23,300
No!

224
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:26,330
- (WHISTLING)
- (BRUCE SCREAMING)

225
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,301
There.

226
00:13:29,242 --> 00:13:30,642
That's better.

227
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:36,415
Mummy always used to say,

228
00:13:36,482 --> 00:13:38,474
"A little pruning
encourages growth."

229
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:43,415
- Where are you taking that?
- Thanks, poppet.

230
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:44,980
BRUCE: Where are
you taking my face?

231
00:13:46,125 --> 00:13:48,492
Please, what's happening to me?

232
00:13:48,995 --> 00:13:50,327
My dear boy,

233
00:13:51,631 --> 00:13:52,894
you're dying.

234
00:13:53,733 --> 00:13:56,168
Just hold still, while
I put these in place.

235
00:13:56,235 --> 00:13:57,669
- BRUCE: No.
- Good Lord.

236
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,503
(BRUCE SCREAMING)

237
00:14:11,484 --> 00:14:14,249
Jim, what a pleasant surprise.

238
00:14:14,354 --> 00:14:16,619
- I'm looking for Selina.
- Haven't seen her.

239
00:14:16,689 --> 00:14:18,681
She's more of an alley
cat than a house cat.

240
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:20,831
- Now I'm just in the middle...
- SOFIA: Let him in.

241
00:14:26,299 --> 00:14:27,323
Hello, James.

242
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,195
It's been a while.

243
00:14:29,836 --> 00:14:31,464
Barbara, can you
give us a moment?

244
00:14:33,172 --> 00:14:34,299
Sure.

245
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:36,706
Have fun, lovebirds.

246
00:14:42,315 --> 00:14:44,147
What is your business
with Barbara Kean?

247
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:46,846
You're worried that I told
her about our arrangement?

248
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:49,784
(CHUCKLES) I know
how to keep a secret.

249
00:14:50,289 --> 00:14:54,385
Now, I want my man Carmichael
released from GCPD custody.

250
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:55,621
That wasn't the deal.

251
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:58,425
You run the underworld.
I run the GCPD.

252
00:14:58,531 --> 00:15:00,727
Your guy got
arrested. That's on him.

253
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,062
Let me make something clear.

254
00:15:03,936 --> 00:15:06,633
Our deal is
whatever I say it is.

255
00:15:06,806 --> 00:15:09,366
Unless you want people
to know you're responsible

256
00:15:09,442 --> 00:15:11,070
for bringing the Pyg to town.

257
00:15:11,811 --> 00:15:13,279
You brought him to Gotham.

258
00:15:13,379 --> 00:15:14,690
I was just trying
to stop Penguin.

259
00:15:14,714 --> 00:15:17,878
But you covered it up and
took credit for killing him.

260
00:15:18,084 --> 00:15:20,246
Word gets out, you're destroyed,

261
00:15:20,353 --> 00:15:22,913
along with your beloved GCPD.

262
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,057
And if I go down,

263
00:15:26,726 --> 00:15:27,726
so will you.

264
00:15:27,794 --> 00:15:29,794
And I think you like being
Queen of the Underworld.

265
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:34,094
(SCOFFS) You still think you
know what I will and won't do?

266
00:15:34,367 --> 00:15:35,960
I know a bluff when I see one.

267
00:15:40,106 --> 00:15:41,267
I have a job to do.

268
00:15:44,544 --> 00:15:45,944
GORDON: Selina.

269
00:15:46,579 --> 00:15:48,741
Hey, Jim, I found
Selina. She went that way.

270
00:15:50,283 --> 00:15:51,842
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

271
00:15:54,921 --> 00:15:57,152
No! No! No!

272
00:15:57,256 --> 00:15:58,622
INMATE: Shut your beak.

273
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:01,519
PENGUIN: No, no!

274
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:03,456
(INMATES CHUCKLING)

275
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:08,628
(GASPING)

276
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:12,270
What do you want?

277
00:16:12,338 --> 00:16:14,637
I told you, Pengy.

278
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:17,836
I'm gonna cure you of
this sad sack mopey act.

279
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:22,278
And the best cure
is the laughing cure.

280
00:16:22,782 --> 00:16:24,114
(LAUGHTER)

281
00:16:25,151 --> 00:16:26,642
Make me laugh.

282
00:16:27,153 --> 00:16:29,520
INMATES: (CHANTING) Make
him laugh! Make him laugh!

283
00:16:29,622 --> 00:16:31,818
So what'll you be performing?

284
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:35,795
Contortionism,
juggling act, a tight five?

285
00:16:35,862 --> 00:16:38,331
Oh. What's that?

286
00:16:39,198 --> 00:16:41,318
- You want to do a clown dance?
- (INMATES EXCLAIMING)

287
00:16:41,434 --> 00:16:43,300
- Yeah!
- Wonderful.

288
00:16:46,472 --> 00:16:48,304
I will not!

289
00:16:48,374 --> 00:16:49,774
INMATES: Ooh.

290
00:16:49,942 --> 00:16:51,001
PENGUIN: No.

291
00:16:52,411 --> 00:16:53,845
Get your hands off. No!

292
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:59,509
INMATES: (CHANTING) Make him
laugh! Make him laugh! Make him laugh!

293
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,182
(SQUEAKER SQUEAKING)

294
00:17:03,155 --> 00:17:04,316
In your own time.

295
00:17:04,390 --> 00:17:05,414
(GRUNTS)

296
00:17:08,528 --> 00:17:10,087
You have no idea
how I've suffered.

297
00:17:11,097 --> 00:17:12,861
The betrayals I've endured.

298
00:17:12,932 --> 00:17:14,833
Just leave me alone.

299
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:17,693
- (SOBBING) Leave me alone!
- Cut!

300
00:17:22,375 --> 00:17:23,570
(SIGHS)

301
00:17:24,343 --> 00:17:26,369
Oswald, Oswald, Oswald.

302
00:17:27,146 --> 00:17:30,173
You are trapped in a prison

303
00:17:30,383 --> 00:17:31,976
in here.

304
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:35,320
And I'm offering you the key.

305
00:17:35,821 --> 00:17:38,086
So, dance!

306
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:41,888
INMATES: (CHANTING) Make him
laugh! Make him laugh! Make him laugh!

307
00:17:42,361 --> 00:17:43,727
Now we're talking.

308
00:17:44,363 --> 00:17:46,889
I can feel the funny
coming. Here it comes!

309
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:49,661
Here comes the funny. Again!

310
00:17:49,769 --> 00:17:50,930
(SCREAMING)

311
00:17:59,445 --> 00:18:01,539
Fred Astaire, you are not.

312
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,078
I'll try again tomorrow.

313
00:18:06,819 --> 00:18:08,151
(CLAMORING)

314
00:18:25,871 --> 00:18:27,100
What the hell, man?

315
00:18:27,206 --> 00:18:28,799
Why were you running, Selina?

316
00:18:28,908 --> 00:18:30,604
'Cause a jerk with a
badge was chasing me.

317
00:18:30,710 --> 00:18:32,554
So not because you were
in Roland Charles' house

318
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:34,274
last night when he
was turned into a tree?

319
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,609
His family saw a
redhead and a brunette.

320
00:18:36,716 --> 00:18:38,981
The brunette was carrying
a leather whip just like yours.

321
00:18:39,085 --> 00:18:40,109
Tell me I'm crazy.

322
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:42,948
I swear, I was only
there to rob the place.

323
00:18:43,255 --> 00:18:44,621
So what about the redhead?

324
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:47,787
She killed some tweaker in
The Narrows the same way.

325
00:18:47,893 --> 00:18:48,952
I need a name.

326
00:18:49,161 --> 00:18:50,959
(SIGHS) Ivy Pepper.

327
00:18:51,497 --> 00:18:52,897
Try again. I know Ivy.

328
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,627
No, Gordon, she's changed.

329
00:18:54,934 --> 00:18:55,934
Like a lot.

330
00:18:56,469 --> 00:18:59,029
She can use plants to hypnotize
people and poison them.

331
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:01,338
So why'd she wanna kill Roland?

332
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,033
'Cause he works for
Wayne Enterprises.

333
00:19:03,342 --> 00:19:04,537
Wayne Enterprise?

334
00:19:04,644 --> 00:19:07,273
She's obsessed with a super
secret project they're doing.

335
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,672
Lucius lied.

336
00:19:09,782 --> 00:19:10,977
Come on, let's go.

337
00:19:18,491 --> 00:19:20,323
Admiring my handiwork?

338
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,160
Excuse me?

339
00:19:25,464 --> 00:19:26,659
Look how beautiful he became.

340
00:19:29,335 --> 00:19:30,826
And all it took

341
00:19:32,004 --> 00:19:34,769
was a little scratch.

342
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,603
What do you want from me?

343
00:19:39,679 --> 00:19:41,671
I wanna know about Project M.

344
00:19:42,948 --> 00:19:44,712
- What is Project M?
- Mmm-mmm.

345
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,341
Bruce Wayne told me everything.

346
00:19:47,353 --> 00:19:49,379
How he didn't even trust
himself with the location

347
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:50,956
but that you know where it is.

348
00:19:53,559 --> 00:19:55,551
And you're gonna take me to it.

349
00:20:00,166 --> 00:20:01,259
But first,

350
00:20:02,835 --> 00:20:04,599
you probably wanna
tell me I'm beautiful.

351
00:20:06,739 --> 00:20:07,832
Yes.

352
00:20:16,582 --> 00:20:17,880
BRUCE: Help.

353
00:20:19,251 --> 00:20:21,379
<i>Help! Somebody help me!</i>

354
00:20:35,534 --> 00:20:37,526
- (INDISTINCT CHATTER)
- (WOMAN CHUCKLING)

355
00:20:37,937 --> 00:20:39,371
Beautiful.

356
00:20:39,438 --> 00:20:41,737
Jim. Jim, you need to help me.

357
00:20:41,841 --> 00:20:43,036
GORDON: Ouch.

358
00:20:43,109 --> 00:20:45,408
Looks like you cut
yourself shaving, old man.

359
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,179
Jim, it's me. It's Bruce.

360
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:49,408
I'm Bruce Wayne.

361
00:20:49,515 --> 00:20:50,710
(BOTH LAUGH)

362
00:20:51,584 --> 00:20:54,019
Honey, I think we'd know
if you were Bruce Wayne.

363
00:20:54,086 --> 00:20:55,577
He's the one
throwing this shindig.

364
00:20:55,688 --> 00:20:57,520
That's him yonder.

365
00:20:58,190 --> 00:21:00,216
WOMAN: Bruce,
you're incorrigible.

366
00:21:00,292 --> 00:21:01,590
I may bust a gut.

367
00:21:02,628 --> 00:21:05,063
- Luckily, I am a doctor.
- (BOTH LAUGH)

368
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:08,158
Ain't he the cat's
pajamas? (LAUGHING)

369
00:21:09,468 --> 00:21:10,731
Go on.

370
00:21:13,973 --> 00:21:15,965
Easy there, sport.

371
00:21:16,075 --> 00:21:17,441
It's Italian velvet.

372
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:19,172
What did you do?
Where's Ra's al Ghul?

373
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:21,239
Ra's al who?

374
00:21:21,347 --> 00:21:22,347
It's my face.

375
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:24,349
He gave you my
face. That's my face.

376
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:26,146
I think you've
been hitting the gin.

377
00:21:26,952 --> 00:21:29,786
Give me back my
face. I'm Bruce Wayne.

378
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,386
Get off of me.

379
00:21:32,458 --> 00:21:33,824
You're ruining my fun.

380
00:21:36,228 --> 00:21:37,662
Everything all right?

381
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:40,392
- Master Bruce?
- Yes, thank you.

382
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:43,292
- Just getting rid of the riffraff.
- (CHICKEN CLUCKING)

383
00:21:51,644 --> 00:21:54,079
Dude, what is it with
you and arm-grabbing?

384
00:21:54,146 --> 00:21:56,809
Harper, I need keys to lockup.
And is Lucius in his office?

385
00:21:56,982 --> 00:21:59,611
Lucius? No, he left
with Ivy a little while ago.

386
00:22:00,152 --> 00:22:03,020
- Ivy Pepper? She was here?
- Yeah.

387
00:22:03,122 --> 00:22:04,954
She asked me to
introduce her to everyone.

388
00:22:05,024 --> 00:22:06,219
Isn't she the coolest?

389
00:22:06,625 --> 00:22:09,220
She's a psycho who turned
a guy into a potted plant.

390
00:22:09,829 --> 00:22:11,161
What's going on with you?

391
00:22:12,531 --> 00:22:14,727
Did he just say
that Ivy's a psycho?

392
00:22:15,134 --> 00:22:16,500
But Ivy's the best.

393
00:22:19,405 --> 00:22:22,204
Is this the hypnosis
I've been hearing about?

394
00:22:22,308 --> 00:22:23,469
I'm gonna say yeah.

395
00:22:23,976 --> 00:22:26,309
Until it fades, they'll
do anything for her.

396
00:22:26,679 --> 00:22:28,341
And think she's the coolest.

397
00:22:31,183 --> 00:22:33,516
What do you mean
by, "Ivy's a psycho"?

398
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:35,845
Hold that thought, Harper.

399
00:22:35,955 --> 00:22:37,446
We'll be right back.

400
00:22:39,058 --> 00:22:40,788
You hear what the
Captain said about Ivy?

401
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:43,659
- But Ivy's awesome.
- Yeah, she is the coolest.

402
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:45,327
(DOOR OPENS IN DISTANCE)

403
00:22:46,131 --> 00:22:47,463
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

404
00:22:53,072 --> 00:22:54,072
(GASPS)

405
00:22:54,206 --> 00:22:56,004
No more! No more!

406
00:22:56,475 --> 00:22:57,738
You have a visitor.

407
00:23:05,784 --> 00:23:07,082
Hello, Oswald.

408
00:23:09,255 --> 00:23:11,019
I see Arkham's
treating you well.

409
00:23:11,357 --> 00:23:12,586
(LAUGHS)

410
00:23:13,259 --> 00:23:14,750
I take it you're here to gloat.

411
00:23:15,194 --> 00:23:16,423
You are correct.

412
00:23:17,596 --> 00:23:19,064
And why not?

413
00:23:20,266 --> 00:23:22,098
I am in an insane asylum,

414
00:23:23,469 --> 00:23:26,132
being pummeled by lunatics.

415
00:23:26,372 --> 00:23:27,635
(CHUCKLING)

416
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:28,969
Then again,

417
00:23:29,208 --> 00:23:30,733
at least I'm not a moron.

418
00:23:32,778 --> 00:23:35,373
I may not be the man I once was.

419
00:23:36,548 --> 00:23:38,608
But I have many things
that you do not have.

420
00:23:38,918 --> 00:23:40,113
A purpose.

421
00:23:40,953 --> 00:23:43,218
Friends. You have
neither of those.

422
00:23:44,189 --> 00:23:45,748
And I wanted you to see that.

423
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:51,222
No.

424
00:23:52,731 --> 00:23:53,731
I know you.

425
00:23:54,800 --> 00:23:58,237
There's something else going on.
Something else brought you here.

426
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:01,702
There's nothing else.

427
00:24:02,574 --> 00:24:05,601
I wanted you to see
how well I am doing.

428
00:24:05,911 --> 00:24:07,641
And I wanted to see
how miserable you are.

429
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:10,105
Mission accomplished. (CHUCKLES)

430
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:11,341
Ed.

431
00:24:13,152 --> 00:24:14,643
I'm going to be
out of here soon.

432
00:24:15,654 --> 00:24:20,592
And once I am, I
am going to wipe

433
00:24:21,026 --> 00:24:23,325
that smile off your face.

434
00:24:24,263 --> 00:24:25,959
Preferably with a chainsaw.

435
00:24:26,131 --> 00:24:28,191
Now, how are you
going to do that?

436
00:24:29,368 --> 00:24:30,996
You have no friends,

437
00:24:31,303 --> 00:24:32,931
no one to help you escape.

438
00:24:34,039 --> 00:24:36,008
You are utterly alone.

439
00:24:38,911 --> 00:24:40,140
Goodbye, Oswald.

440
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:45,614
Sorry, but I don't
put too much stock

441
00:24:45,684 --> 00:24:48,119
in the opinions of simpletons!

442
00:24:48,187 --> 00:24:49,450
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

443
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:06,828
"I am held captive all day,
my brilliance locked away.

444
00:25:07,373 --> 00:25:10,207
"This prison must
be broken. The key?

445
00:25:13,212 --> 00:25:15,010
"My name which must be spoken."

446
00:25:20,019 --> 00:25:21,817
You're still in there.

447
00:25:24,923 --> 00:25:26,551
That's why you came.

448
00:25:27,826 --> 00:25:29,385
You're still there.

449
00:25:30,329 --> 00:25:32,209
And you're gonna help
me find a way out of here.

450
00:25:33,399 --> 00:25:35,891
Hello? We should be leaving.

451
00:25:36,001 --> 00:25:38,232
Not until we find out
where Ivy took Lucius.

452
00:25:38,337 --> 00:25:39,532
There has to be something.

453
00:25:50,349 --> 00:25:52,841
IVY: <i>You know where it is and
you are going to take me to it.</i>

454
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:55,744
LUCIUS: <i>Mmm.
You're so incredible.</i>

455
00:25:56,155 --> 00:25:59,819
IVY: <i>Uh-huh. Where is Project M?</i>

456
00:25:59,892 --> 00:26:02,657
LUCIUS: <i>Wayne Biotech has
a secret facility outside the city</i>

457
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:04,390
<i>at the edge of Kane Park.</i>

458
00:26:04,863 --> 00:26:06,058
Good man, Lucius.

459
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:08,325
COP: <i>In here.</i>

460
00:26:09,268 --> 00:26:12,170
Hey, Cap, the boys
and I were talking,

461
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,515
and we didn't
really like the way

462
00:26:13,539 --> 00:26:14,871
that you were talking about Ivy.

463
00:26:14,940 --> 00:26:16,909
I told you we should've left.

464
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:21,070
Look, I think you
misinterpreted what I was saying.

465
00:26:22,614 --> 00:26:24,242
You called Ivy a psycho.

466
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:26,545
That's a term of endearment.

467
00:26:26,785 --> 00:26:29,118
I love Ivy. I think she's great.

468
00:26:29,588 --> 00:26:30,920
What about you?

469
00:26:31,256 --> 00:26:32,280
Do you love Ivy?

470
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:35,587
Yeah, I love Ivy.

471
00:26:37,429 --> 00:26:38,727
How much?

472
00:26:38,797 --> 00:26:42,734
I love Ivy so much that
I wish I could be her.

473
00:26:45,137 --> 00:26:46,765
You're not really selling it.

474
00:26:47,106 --> 00:26:48,438
And you think you did?

475
00:26:48,974 --> 00:26:50,272
Run.

476
00:26:50,642 --> 00:26:51,803
HARPER: Get them!

477
00:26:54,413 --> 00:26:55,608
Selina!

478
00:27:05,390 --> 00:27:06,722
(SNORING)

479
00:27:08,594 --> 00:27:09,994
(KEY JINGLING)

480
00:27:10,095 --> 00:27:11,961
(DOOR OPENS)

481
00:27:20,272 --> 00:27:23,367
All right, Oswald,
old buddy, old pal.

482
00:27:23,775 --> 00:27:25,869
Tonight, we're gonna cure you.

483
00:27:26,445 --> 00:27:28,175
Make me laugh or else.

484
00:27:28,714 --> 00:27:33,209
Let's call this the
sudden death round.

485
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:36,147
(SNIFFS)

486
00:27:39,124 --> 00:27:40,217
Dietrich?

487
00:27:44,897 --> 00:27:46,593
(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)

488
00:27:51,637 --> 00:27:54,163
Okay, that was clever-ish.

489
00:27:58,610 --> 00:28:00,101
Yeah, that's a spoon.

490
00:28:00,612 --> 00:28:02,012
It is also a fork!

491
00:28:02,114 --> 00:28:04,015
Looks like you got
some fight in you still.

492
00:28:04,116 --> 00:28:07,644
But it's just too
little, too late, too...

493
00:28:07,953 --> 00:28:11,481
(SIGHS) Boring.
Lobotomize the little bird.

494
00:28:11,790 --> 00:28:13,452
Wait. Wait.

495
00:28:14,626 --> 00:28:17,653
You said this prison
was all in my mind.

496
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:22,362
Maybe I'm in a prison right now.

497
00:28:22,434 --> 00:28:26,496
A prison where
you can't get to me.

498
00:28:40,085 --> 00:28:41,451
(CHUCKLES)

499
00:28:42,788 --> 00:28:44,051
Okay.

500
00:28:46,358 --> 00:28:48,054
You really are nuts.

501
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:53,259
(INMATES EXCLAIM)

502
00:28:54,199 --> 00:28:55,667
(GRUNTS)

503
00:28:58,370 --> 00:28:59,736
(GRUNTING)

504
00:29:17,222 --> 00:29:18,781
(FAINT LAUGHTER)

505
00:29:27,499 --> 00:29:29,092
(GRUNTING)

506
00:29:31,136 --> 00:29:32,934
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

507
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:37,599
Try laughing now,
you ginger sap!

508
00:29:38,176 --> 00:29:39,667
Yes!

509
00:29:44,916 --> 00:29:49,183
(CACKLING)

510
00:29:49,521 --> 00:29:52,650
See? I told you I'd cure you.

511
00:29:52,758 --> 00:29:54,624
Don't flatter yourself!

512
00:29:54,726 --> 00:29:56,058
One more.

513
00:29:57,562 --> 00:29:58,996
(CACKLING)

514
00:30:02,434 --> 00:30:04,903
And so I said to the guy...
You wanna know what I said?

515
00:30:05,404 --> 00:30:07,305
I said, "What is this?

516
00:30:07,406 --> 00:30:08,897
"A three-ring circus?"

517
00:30:08,974 --> 00:30:10,567
(ALL LAUGHING)

518
00:30:13,578 --> 00:30:15,444
And keep them coming.

519
00:30:23,221 --> 00:30:25,656
How long do you think
you can hide in here?

520
00:30:26,892 --> 00:30:28,053
Look.

521
00:30:29,294 --> 00:30:30,660
Out there.

522
00:30:32,030 --> 00:30:33,726
He's going to find
you eventually.

523
00:30:35,567 --> 00:30:36,899
I don't understand.

524
00:30:37,002 --> 00:30:38,129
Who's going to find me?

525
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:45,902
(HELICOPTER HOVERING)

526
00:30:50,349 --> 00:30:51,408
Alfred?

527
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:53,951
Special Agent Pennyworth
to you, you scumbag!

528
00:30:54,953 --> 00:30:57,286
The kid's secured,
requesting extraction.

529
00:30:57,789 --> 00:30:59,018
No!

530
00:31:06,365 --> 00:31:07,697
Just be careful, here.

531
00:31:08,300 --> 00:31:09,632
We're gonna go this way.

532
00:31:12,471 --> 00:31:13,495
This way.

533
00:31:19,644 --> 00:31:20,644
So this is it.

534
00:31:21,980 --> 00:31:23,471
Project M.

535
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:30,113
Also called "Lazarus Water."

536
00:31:30,689 --> 00:31:32,885
It belonged to a man
known as Ra's al Ghul.

537
00:31:32,958 --> 00:31:35,621
It stimulates cell growth
at an alarming rate.

538
00:31:36,128 --> 00:31:37,619
We've yet to figure out how.

539
00:31:40,866 --> 00:31:43,893
I assumed Project M killed
plants, but it's the opposite.

540
00:31:46,304 --> 00:31:49,900
Just like humans to lock
up something so beautiful.

541
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:51,972
What are you
going to do with it?

542
00:31:54,813 --> 00:31:57,044
I'm going to make
miracles happen.

543
00:32:10,028 --> 00:32:11,553
Release me!

544
00:32:14,099 --> 00:32:17,092
Listen to me. I'm Bruce Wayne. I
can pay you whatever you want.

545
00:32:17,202 --> 00:32:18,568
You need to let me go now!

546
00:32:18,637 --> 00:32:20,367
Sorry, I can't do
that now, love.

547
00:32:20,639 --> 00:32:23,268
- You see, I have a mission.
- What mission?

548
00:32:23,608 --> 00:32:26,100
For me to bring you to him.

549
00:32:29,981 --> 00:32:31,449
What is that?

550
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:34,750
Well, giddy up, son.

551
00:32:55,941 --> 00:32:57,466
What do you want?

552
00:32:58,009 --> 00:32:59,272
Why did you bring me here?

553
00:32:59,344 --> 00:33:01,336
This is where my
parents were killed!

554
00:33:01,446 --> 00:33:02,607
SHADOW: No.

555
00:33:03,248 --> 00:33:05,342
This is where I was born.

556
00:33:10,088 --> 00:33:11,579
No!

557
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:20,924
That's far enough.

558
00:33:24,803 --> 00:33:25,930
Jim Gordon.

559
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:27,302
Ivy Pepper.

560
00:33:27,372 --> 00:33:28,840
IVY: It's been a long time.

561
00:33:29,407 --> 00:33:31,501
I'm not the same
kid you remember.

562
00:33:32,744 --> 00:33:35,213
The kid who's father
you and you partner killed

563
00:33:35,313 --> 00:33:36,372
all those years ago?

564
00:33:38,350 --> 00:33:39,350
How is this possible?

565
00:33:40,318 --> 00:33:42,651
Well, first, I was a seed.

566
00:33:43,655 --> 00:33:45,248
Then a sprout.

567
00:33:46,358 --> 00:33:47,826
Now I've bloomed.

568
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:49,660
Drop your gun.

569
00:33:51,196 --> 00:33:54,496
Or your friend Lucius
becomes a flower arrangement.

570
00:34:03,975 --> 00:34:05,637
Lucius, you okay?

571
00:34:06,645 --> 00:34:09,376
I'm in the sweet embrace of
one of my favorite people, Jim.

572
00:34:09,748 --> 00:34:10,748
Never been better.

573
00:34:11,550 --> 00:34:13,143
Now I know you're tenacious,

574
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:14,914
Jim Gordon, gun or no gun.

575
00:34:15,220 --> 00:34:16,882
You'll come after me.

576
00:34:17,522 --> 00:34:18,581
But then,

577
00:34:19,724 --> 00:34:21,317
Bruce Wayne will die.

578
00:34:22,894 --> 00:34:23,934
What have you done to him?

579
00:34:23,995 --> 00:34:26,260
I went to Wayne Manor
and planted a seed.

580
00:34:27,032 --> 00:34:29,365
I imagine he's about to bloom.

581
00:34:29,434 --> 00:34:30,902
But if you let me go,

582
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:34,635
you may have a chance

583
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:36,736
to get him the antidote.

584
00:34:41,379 --> 00:34:42,642
This isn't over.

585
00:34:42,881 --> 00:34:44,975
You have no idea
how right you are.

586
00:34:46,384 --> 00:34:47,613
I love you.

587
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:51,052
Lucius, give me the antidote.

588
00:34:51,122 --> 00:34:54,058
Let's just wait until Ivy
is at a safe distance.

589
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:55,593
Give me the antidote. Come on.

590
00:34:57,062 --> 00:34:58,826
- Don't make me hit you.
- Jim.

591
00:34:59,230 --> 00:35:01,825
I must warn you, I'm
a black belt in jiu-jitsu.

592
00:35:02,133 --> 00:35:03,133
Since when?

593
00:35:03,301 --> 00:35:04,301
Night classes.

594
00:35:11,977 --> 00:35:13,741
- The Lazarus Water.
- Come on.

595
00:35:13,812 --> 00:35:16,077
We've got to get to
Bruce Wayne. Let's go.

596
00:35:18,083 --> 00:35:19,949
(BATS SQUEAKING)

597
00:35:41,373 --> 00:35:42,534
Help!

598
00:35:45,043 --> 00:35:46,705
Somebody help!

599
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:47,835
(WINGS FLAPPING)

600
00:35:49,381 --> 00:35:50,679
Who's there?

601
00:35:51,483 --> 00:35:52,712
(SQUEAKING CONTINUES)

602
00:35:52,851 --> 00:35:54,114
Show yourself!

603
00:36:01,660 --> 00:36:03,026
Who are you?

604
00:36:05,163 --> 00:36:08,156
SHADOW: I am the
one you cannot escape.

605
00:36:08,933 --> 00:36:11,767
The one you cannot kill.

606
00:36:14,539 --> 00:36:15,666
You're me?

607
00:36:17,776 --> 00:36:19,438
- Please...
- SHADOW: You're scared.

608
00:36:19,511 --> 00:36:20,877
You should be.

609
00:36:24,816 --> 00:36:25,943
(GASPS)

610
00:36:26,117 --> 00:36:27,210
(PANTING)

611
00:36:27,352 --> 00:36:29,218
It's okay, Bruce.
It's all right.

612
00:36:30,121 --> 00:36:31,145
You're safe now.

613
00:36:42,567 --> 00:36:43,865
According to Lucius,

614
00:36:43,935 --> 00:36:46,928
Ivy's toxin attacks the
brain like a hallucinogen.

615
00:36:48,039 --> 00:36:50,440
So whatever you went through,

616
00:36:50,542 --> 00:36:52,204
I doubt it was pleasant,

617
00:36:52,444 --> 00:36:53,776
but it wasn't real.

618
00:36:55,714 --> 00:36:57,114
I think I saw who I really am.

619
00:37:00,852 --> 00:37:02,115
I know what you're gonna say.

620
00:37:02,954 --> 00:37:05,355
But what I saw, it was real.

621
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:09,190
Well, then you're lucky.

622
00:37:10,662 --> 00:37:12,506
Most people go their
whole lives not ever knowing

623
00:37:12,530 --> 00:37:14,130
- who they really are...
- I'm not lucky.

624
00:37:14,899 --> 00:37:16,162
You didn't see it.

625
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:25,274
I've seen my own darkness.

626
00:37:27,779 --> 00:37:28,838
I'll say this.

627
00:37:29,714 --> 00:37:32,741
You have people around
you who care for you.

628
00:37:34,786 --> 00:37:35,947
Don't fight this alone.

629
00:37:36,454 --> 00:37:37,581
Trust us.

630
00:37:40,658 --> 00:37:41,956
I'll leave men outside tonight.

631
00:37:42,627 --> 00:37:44,892
I'll come by tomorrow,
check in on you.

632
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:48,265
Jim.

633
00:37:50,101 --> 00:37:51,125
When I was under,

634
00:37:52,303 --> 00:37:53,396
I saw you.

635
00:37:54,973 --> 00:37:56,305
You had a mustache.

636
00:38:01,346 --> 00:38:03,406
Well, clearly, that's a
very dangerous toxin.

637
00:38:11,956 --> 00:38:12,956
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

638
00:38:20,598 --> 00:38:22,794
Alfred, it's...

639
00:38:22,901 --> 00:38:24,392
It's me. It's Bruce. I...

640
00:38:28,573 --> 00:38:29,836
I need your help, Alfred.

641
00:38:31,743 --> 00:38:32,904
Please call me.

642
00:38:33,511 --> 00:38:35,605
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)
- (RAIN PATTERING)

643
00:38:47,358 --> 00:38:48,690
We're not hypnotized.

644
00:38:48,793 --> 00:38:50,193
Just embarrassed.

645
00:38:52,730 --> 00:38:53,730
Good to have you back.

646
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,498
All right, listen up.

647
00:38:57,135 --> 00:38:59,661
I want an APB on Ivy Pepper.

648
00:38:59,737 --> 00:39:01,682
- Finding her is our top priority.
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)

649
00:39:01,706 --> 00:39:04,005
All right, you heard him,
people. Let's get to work.

650
00:39:05,910 --> 00:39:08,122
- What do you want?
- SOFIA: <i>I thought about what you said.</i>

651
00:39:08,146 --> 00:39:11,947
How if I used the Pyg to destroy
you, I'd also destroy myself.

652
00:39:12,016 --> 00:39:13,211
GORDON: <i>And?</i>

653
00:39:13,484 --> 00:39:14,679
And

654
00:39:14,786 --> 00:39:16,049
you're right.

655
00:39:16,621 --> 00:39:18,954
I've come to enjoy being
the Queen of Gotham.

656
00:39:19,123 --> 00:39:20,323
Glad we understand each other.

657
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:23,487
SOFIA: <i>Not quite. You see, I
also realized I don't need the Pyg.</i>

658
00:39:25,463 --> 00:39:28,023
There are other ways
for me to hurt you.

659
00:39:35,573 --> 00:39:37,201
Thank you so much for coming.

660
00:39:37,675 --> 00:39:39,644
I thought we were
overdue for a chat.

661
00:39:40,144 --> 00:39:42,045
How could I say no
to my sister-in-law?

662
00:39:44,682 --> 00:39:46,378
(RAIN PATTERING)

663
00:39:47,585 --> 00:39:49,178
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

664
00:39:53,925 --> 00:39:56,417
JOKER: <i>So I strangled
him with his lower intestines.</i>

665
00:40:01,566 --> 00:40:03,125
Relax, buddy.

666
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:05,093
You gave me what I needed.

667
00:40:05,203 --> 00:40:07,536
The laugh of the century.

668
00:40:12,744 --> 00:40:13,939
Tell me something.

669
00:40:14,612 --> 00:40:16,877
You appear to have everyone
here under your thumb,

670
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:19,607
- the guards, the inmates...
- What can I say?

671
00:40:19,717 --> 00:40:21,379
I'm a charismatic guy.

672
00:40:23,721 --> 00:40:25,189
You could escape anytime.

673
00:40:25,423 --> 00:40:26,914
- Why stay?
- Hmm.

674
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:30,425
Why indeed?

675
00:40:32,263 --> 00:40:35,859
- You're planning something.
- JOKER: Righty, old boy.

676
00:40:36,367 --> 00:40:41,271
Something spectacular.

677
00:40:41,372 --> 00:40:43,136
See, I'm in this funny farm

678
00:40:43,241 --> 00:40:46,177
'cause I need to find
the <i>crème de la</i> crazy,

679
00:40:50,415 --> 00:40:52,179
which is why I need you.

680
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:57,183
(BOTH LAUGHING)

681
00:41:00,191 --> 00:41:01,682
Ah, you get it.

682
00:41:01,793 --> 00:41:04,262
But when we're done,

683
00:41:04,963 --> 00:41:09,298
the world out there,
that'll be the asylum.

684
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:11,629
What do you say?

685
00:41:14,172 --> 00:41:16,266
Thank you for your kind offer.

686
00:41:18,576 --> 00:41:21,068
I don't expect to
be here very long.

687
00:41:28,753 --> 00:41:30,745
You'll come around.

688
00:41:32,123 --> 00:41:34,149
They always do.

689
00:41:39,931 --> 00:41:41,126
(WHISTLING)

690
00:41:46,004 --> 00:41:47,131
Nope.

691
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:21,172
Where did these
plants come from?

692
00:42:21,406 --> 00:42:22,567
Get out!

693
00:42:22,673 --> 00:42:24,369
Before we call the police.

694
00:42:41,926 --> 00:42:43,588
(COUGHING)

695
00:42:53,538 --> 00:42:54,801
Oh, friends.

696
00:42:55,873 --> 00:42:58,206
You're all so beautiful.

697
00:43:39,484 --> 00:43:40,543
English - SDH
